    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you're saying about blood pressure, but i feel like i know my body pretty well. i've always eaten these foods and i've never had a spike or anything. i'm mostly just worried about the nutrition side of things. since you're a wellness guide, can you just give me a definitive yes or no? like, if i keep the portions moderate and eat my veggies, am i actually at risk of something life-threatening, or is it just a minor thing i should keep an eye on? i'd rather just know now so i can stop stressing about it.",
